//
// Expected: a sanity error naming HKDF. A key derivation function protects
// nothing on its own — its output is only as secret as its input — so there is
// no confidentiality guarantee to declare broken, and `weak` on it is a
// modelling mistake rather than a weaker model. The diagnostic has to say so:
// an assumption that silently did nothing would read as a check that was
// performed.

attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	knows private ikm
	knows public salt, info
	k_one, k_two, k_three = HKDF[weak](salt, ikm, info)
]

Alice -> Bob: k_one

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(k_one)
]

queries[
	confidentiality? ikm
]
